{"packet":3,"rowIndex":0,"value":{"evidence":[{"path":"outputs/locale-assets-20261026/es-419/workflow-v3-completion-20261030/0076-work/actor-original-context.jsonl","sha256":"43c6e5fd58a692e877f458311fcbff113e56c53644d966fc3fa04673f8c5e919"},{"path":"localization/source/bgdatabase-20261027/actor-identity/ADAPTER.md","sha256":"408a7480d79ddc43c9cdad7279b732634daacbcfb546246743b6f46513ab60be"},{"path":"localization/source/bgdatabase-20261027/actor-identity/nameplate.il","sha256":"12953ce7468aafeac4557f99e92bbf7fb337aafd7dad94b521a8c8ce6e3775c8"}],"id":"semantic-context:actor-defaults","primaryFamily":"actor","rules":["Keep the46 exact sheet/row/field identities and195 fixed identity/control states. Do not invent32 absent values.","Approved full names and short names are distinct: retain both forms exactly as bound. Fisher is the original displayed name for internal Fish; Fen uses plugin key wolf. Neither key becomes translated display text.","Eight generic Mouse labels remain Ratón: grammatical noun gender assigns no canonical gender or adjective/pronoun. Do not expand them to glossary personality labels. Plant stays Planta; Charlotte in-bed is its own original row.","Ordinary nonintroduced nameplates show ???. Start-menu and instanced-story bypasses, custom nameplate precedence and current BioDetail override behavior remain the accepted source implementation. No reveal timing or lookup keys are edited.","Fisher/Forest mice remain without invented gender; MabelsMom remains the female kinship label Mamá de Mabel. FullName getter anomaly is preserved."],"source":"The original Actor39 table has46 nonempty default display cells and32 absent cells. Internal name/savekey/plugin_db_name and flags are separate unchanged controls. Defaults are not the introduction state."}}
{"packet":3,"rowIndex":1,"value":{"evidence":[{"path":"outputs/locale-assets-20261026/es-419/workflow-v3-completion-20261030/0076-work/notebook-five-pages.jsonl","sha256":"772bfe3e942a006ee7f14152b29cfbc50b64b829f0b75ed87c93f500572ca74c"},{"path":"outputs/locale-assets-20261026/es-419/workflow-v3-completion-20261030/0076-work/notebook-field-outputs.jsonl","sha256":"5fd784906248b63372e78e3add775cf2a44c149b3be9c0440caf3ac93d0cbf2b"},{"path":"localization/source/notebook-tutorial-ui-20261027/layout.json","sha256":"ba8000d39f6eb78470470c4fada21e7577d23188583ef45b5fb1b9939ee07ca7"},{"path":"localization/source/notebook-tutorial-ui-20261027/artwork-bindings.json","sha256":"0afceb16ee276baa5c8ed12a6179377f579a1c32a355ec586b811f601af566a9"}],"id":"semantic-context:notebook-pages","primaryFamily":"notebook","rules":["Read all five complete pages and every primary source/target field. The26 page fields include accepted title context; do not count that context as new primary review.","Preserve exact LF/CRLF/CR sequence and terminal separators, including details terminal CR and talk terminal CRLF. The shared renderer restores per-field original separators.","Use original action words TALK/GOSSIP. Chismes is the glossary concept; no new image/artwork is generated.","Complete-title variant replaces split-position layout in the accepted shared mechanism. First L and remainder IBRETA are separate authored components; they are not proof that the English manual positions form a valid target title. Preserve independent full-title and glow IDs.","Page order: acquisition; TALK/GOSSIP distinction; discoveries/options over time; current/completed quest storage and upper-left tracking; character information and hidden details. No layout/renderer/runtime acceptance here."],"source":"GossipTutorialRedux15851 exposes five ordered pages. TALK/GOSSIP are the actual unchanged English sprite labels. Six face/glow components per field are independent overlay components."}}
{"packet":3,"rowIndex":2,"value":{"evidence":[{"path":"outputs/locale-assets-20261026/es-419/workflow-v3-completion-20261030/0076-work/tutorial-field-outputs.jsonl","sha256":"e6fcec7d7c176093426fd5dc5486e236ab36d3ae8a51b36e04e56b2285b0ec24"},{"path":"outputs/locale-assets-20261026/es-419/workflow-v3-completion-20261030/0076-work/tutorial-source-context.jsonl","sha256":"0cdbef68e2d77a567e29ede3a513e3f4004d1a7313468d00f1d33e5436eef8e8"},{"path":"localization/source/tutorial-quest-ru-20261027/plan.json","sha256":"9a94aa6a554bed1a7e6f9b30196004da63b724ece5651da6e8e2e54a11b65e73"},{"path":"localization/source/bgdatabase-20261027/quest-progress/decoded.json","sha256":"b311611c705966e636cd4328c4e7d65595be7ed4dfeab58fad7bc69e2528bff1"}],"id":"semantic-context:tutorial-order-and-referent","primaryFamily":"tutorial","rules":["Read all six fields in order: title, overall objective, greeting bunny, ask Maverick for sugar, return quoted sugar to Scarlett, meet nearby critters. All six are primary; old0011/0037 context judgments are not primary acceptance.","The one correction is Saluda al conejo. -> Saluda a la coneja. The female species label preserves source anonymity and does not insert Scarlett’s name in the instruction.","Retain the Sugar/lubricant misunderstanding and quoted return object. Do not replace sugar with lubricant or reveal the joke early. Scarlett remains beneficiary/recipient; Maverick remains supplier.","Current and completed mission terminology remains distinct from dates and character names; use Azúcar y especias from the approved glossary."],"source":"Original Quest Act1_TutorialQuest starts at progress0. The original conversation act1/tutorialQuest/01_introFromBunny names Scarlett at ds:120:152, Actor2, and has her send Rascal to Maverick for sugar at ds:120:180/186. The source actor/glossary binds Scarlett as female."}}
